# DTF tier manifest: upload-commit-records  (artifact-keeper#6383, #6346,
# #6318; 1.13.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. HTTP plus DB truth (docker exec psql
# against this slot's Postgres, DB_CONTAINER). No egress, no object storage.
#
# THE PROBLEM
#   (#6383) Several upload paths wrote the format metadata a package is served
#   from AFTER the artifact row committed, and only logged (or discarded) a
#   failure there: a generic PUT of a package into a PyPI, Debian or RPM
#   repository, the native RPM upload, the NuGet push. Under pool exhaustion
#   the package was then stored without its metadata row: out of its format's
#   index, and its retry refused with 409. A versioning-enabled Generic
#   repository appended the revision after the commit too, so a failure there
#   answered an error for an upload that had replaced the HEAD.
#   (#6346, #6318) The PyPI upload (and NuGet, Debian, nested RPM and the
#   generic PUT's native finalize) upserted its package catalog row twice:
#   once in the upload service's finalize, again in the handler. Every write is
#   a pool checkout; per-upload connection demand is what a small pool runs out
#   of.
#
# THE FIX (1.13.0)
#   The metadata document and the revision commit in the transaction that
#   commits the artifact row (a failure rolls the upload back, so the error is
#   true and the retry starts clean); the handler that registers the catalog
#   row tells the upload service, which then writes none of its own.
#
# THE PRIMITIVES
#   * Fault injection: a BEFORE INSERT OR UPDATE trigger on artifact_metadata
#     (and one on artifact_versions) raises for rows naming the marker
#     `dtfw13ufault` while a switch row is set. Only this tier's packages carry
#     the marker; the oracle drops the triggers on exit.
#   * Write counting: AFTER INSERT OR UPDATE row triggers on packages and
#     package_versions log each row write with the package name.
#
# Oracle (RELEASE_GATE=1):
#   (FIX #6383) with the metadata write failing, a generic PUT of a wheel into
#     a PyPI repository, a NuGet push and a native RPM upload each leave no
#     live artifact row without its metadata. RED on main: 201 and a stored
#     package with no artifact_metadata row.
#   (FIX #6383) the same uploads, retried with the fault cleared, are 2xx with
#     metadata. RED on main: 409, the first attempt holds the path.
#   (FIX #6383) on a versioning-enabled generic repository, a replacement
#     whose revision write fails leaves the HEAD serving the previous bytes.
#     RED on main: the HEAD already serves the new bytes.
#   (FIX #6346) a twine-style PyPI upload and a NuGet push each write their
#     packages row twice (insert, update) and package_versions once. RED on
#     main: four packages writes.
#   (FIX #6318) a generic PUT of a wheel into a PyPI repository writes the
#     catalog once. RED on main: the finalize and the native record both write.
#   (CONTROL) the uploaded project is listed in the simple index with its
#     summary; the catalog row carries the description (green on both).
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
COVERS="6383 6346 6318"
